-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, ss 259 to 261 -- WHAT A MERGER OR CONSOLIDATION DOES, WHAT THE SURVIVING CORPORATION MAY
-- DO, AND WHAT A MERGER AGREEMENT MAY PROVIDE.
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N.
--
-- Section 259 states the effects of a merger or consolidation that "shall have become effective under this chapter" (the time of effect is
-- s 103's, piece dg1: a plain input here). Section 260 says what the surviving or resulting corporation (or the converted or domesticated one) may
-- do to finance and carry out the transaction. Section 261 says what an agreement of merger under s 251 may provide (penalties for failing to
-- close; a stockholder representative) and that pending actions continue.
-- The effects are statements about what follows once the transaction is effective, so each is a BOOLEAN rule of the facts "it is effective"
-- (and, where the text distinguishes, "this is the surviving corporation"). Nothing here is a duty with a deadline.

§ `s 259 Status, rights and liabilities after a merger or consolidation`

-- (a) "When any merger or consolidation shall have become effective under this chapter, for all purposes of the laws of this State the
-- separate existence of all the constituent corporations, or of all such constituent corporations except the one into which the other or
-- others of such constituent corporations have been merged, as the case may be, shall cease and the constituent corporations shall become a new
-- corporation, or be merged into 1 of such corporations, as the case may be, possessing all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises ...".
-- src:1231 | (a) When any merger or consolidation shall have become effective under this chapter, for all purposes of the laws of this State the separate existence of all the constituent corporations, or of all such constituent corporations except the one into which the other or others of such constituent corporations have been merged, as the case may be, shall cease and the constituent corporations shall become a new corporation, or be merged into 1 of such corporations, as the case may be, possessing all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises as well of a public as of a private nature …
-- src:1231 | and all and singular, the rights, privileges, powers and franchises of each of said corporations, and all property, real, personal and mixed, and all debts due to any of said constituent corporations on whatever account, as well for stock subscriptions as all other things in action or belonging to each of such corporations shall be vested in the corporation surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation …
-- src:1231 | and the title to any real estate vested by deed or otherwise, under the laws of this State, in any of such constituent corporations, shall not revert or be in any way impaired by reason of this chapter …
-- src:1231 | but all rights of creditors and all liens upon any property of any of said constituent corporations shall be preserved unimpaired, and all debts, liabilities and duties of the respective constituent corporations shall thenceforth attach to said surviving or resulting corporation, and may be enforced against it to the same extent as if said debts, liabilities and duties had been incurred or contracted by it …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 259(a) (src:1231)
DECLARE `s 259(a) Effect of a merger or consolidation` IS ONE OF
    `the separate existence of the constituent corporation ceases`
    `the constituent corporations become a new corporation, or are merged into one of them`
    `the surviving or resulting corporation has all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises, and is subject to all the restrictions, disabilities and duties, of each constituent corporation`
    `all property, debts due and things in action of each constituent corporation are vested in the surviving or resulting corporation`
    `title to real estate vested in a constituent corporation does not revert and is not impaired by reason of this chapter`
    `the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of a constituent corporation are preserved unimpaired`
    `the debts, liabilities and duties of a constituent corporation attach to the surviving or resulting corporation and may be enforced against it as if it had incurred them`

-- src:1231 | (a) When any merger or consolidation shall have become effective under this chapter, for all purposes of the laws of this State the separate existence of all the constituent corporations, or of all such constituent corporations except the one into which the other or others of such constituent corporations have been merged, as the case may be, shall cease and the constituent corporations shall become a new corporation, or be merged into 1 of such corporations, as the case may be, possessing all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises as well of a public as of a private nature …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 259(a) (src:1231)
DECLARE `s 259 Status of a merger or consolidation` HAS
    `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`                      IS A BOOLEAN   -- the time of effect is s 103's (piece dg1)
    `the constituent corporation concerned is the one into which the others have been merged`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The separate existence of a constituent corporation ceases, except the one into which the others are merged. Every other effect follows
-- from the transaction having become effective.
-- src:1231 | (a) When any merger or consolidation shall have become effective under this chapter, for all purposes of the laws of this State the separate existence of all the constituent corporations, or of all such constituent corporations except the one into which the other or others of such constituent corporations have been merged, as the case may be, shall cease and the constituent corporations shall become a new corporation, or be merged into 1 of such corporations, as the case may be, possessing all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises as well of a public as of a private nature, and being subject to all the restrictions, disabilities and duties of each of such corporations so merged or consolidated; and all and singular, the rights, privileges, powers and franchises of each of said corporations, and all property, real, personal and mixed, and all debts due to any of said constituent corporations on whatever account, as well for stock subscriptions as all other things in action or belonging to each of such corporations shall be vested in the corporation surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation; and all property, rights, privileges, powers and franchises, and all and every other interest shall be thereafter as effectually the property of the surviving or resulting corporation as they were of the several and respective constituent corporations, and the title to any real estate vested by deed or otherwise, under the laws of this State, in any of such constituent corporations, shall not revert or be in any way impaired by reason of this chapter; but all rights of creditors and all liens upon any property of any of said constituent corporations shall be preserved unimpaired, and all debts, liabilities and duties of the respective constituent corporations shall thenceforth attach to said surviving or resulting corporation, and may be enforced against it to the same extent as if said debts, liabilities and duties had been incurred or contracted by it …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 259(a) (src:1231)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 259(a) Effect of a merger or consolidation`
      status IS A `s 259 Status of a merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 259(a) the effect follows` effect status MEANS
    CONSIDER effect
    WHEN `the separate existence of the constituent corporation ceases` THEN
            status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
        AND (NOT status's `the constituent corporation concerned is the one into which the others have been merged`)
    WHEN `the constituent corporations become a new corporation, or are merged into one of them`                                                                                    THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
    WHEN `the surviving or resulting corporation has all the rights, privileges, powers and franchises, and is subject to all the restrictions, disabilities and duties, of each constituent corporation` THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
    WHEN `all property, debts due and things in action of each constituent corporation are vested in the surviving or resulting corporation`                                         THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
    WHEN `title to real estate vested in a constituent corporation does not revert and is not impaired by reason of this chapter`                                                    THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
    WHEN `the rights of creditors and the liens upon the property of a constituent corporation are preserved unimpaired`                                                              THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`
    WHEN `the debts, liabilities and duties of a constituent corporation attach to the surviving or resulting corporation and may be enforced against it as if it had incurred them`  THEN status's `the merger or consolidation has become effective under this chapter`

-- (b) "In the case of a merger of banks or trust companies, without any order or action on the part of any court or otherwise, all
-- appointments, designations, and nominations, and all other rights and interests as trustee, executor, administrator, registrar of stocks and
-- bonds, guardian of estates, assignee, receiver, trustee of estates of persons mentally ill and in every other fiduciary capacity, shall be
-- automatically vested in the corporation resulting from or surviving such merger".
-- src:1232 | (b) In the case of a merger of banks or trust companies, without any order or action on the part of any court or otherwise, all appointments, designations, and nominations, and all other rights and interests as trustee, executor, administrator, registrar of stocks and bonds, guardian of estates, assignee, receiver, trustee of estates of persons mentally ill and in every other fiduciary capacity, shall be automatically vested in the corporation resulting from or surviving such merger …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 259(b) (src:1232)
GIVEN `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merger has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 259(b) the fiduciary appointments and interests vest automatically in the corporation resulting from or surviving the merger` `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` `the merger has become effective` MEANS
        `it is a merger of banks or trust companies`
    AND `the merger has become effective`

-- "provided, however, that any party in interest shall have the right to apply to an appropriate court or tribunal for a determination as to
-- whether the surviving corporation shall continue to serve in the same fiduciary capacity as the merged corporation, or whether a new and
-- different fiduciary should be appointed." The determination is the court's: not a rule here.
-- src:1232 | provided, however, that any party in interest shall have the right to apply to an appropriate court or tribunal for a determination as to whether the surviving corporation shall continue to serve in the same fiduciary capacity as the merged corporation, or whether a new and different fiduciary should be appointed …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 259(b) (src:1232)
GIVEN `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a party in interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 259(b) the person has the right to apply to a court or tribunal for a determination of the fiduciary` `it is a merger of banks or trust companies` `the person is a party in interest` MEANS
        `it is a merger of banks or trust companies`
    AND `the person is a party in interest`

§ `s 260 Powers of the surviving or resulting corporation; issuance of stock, bonds and other indebtedness`

-- (a) "When 2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes
-- domesticated as, a corporation of this State, the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation or upon conversion or
-- domestication may issue bonds or other obligations, negotiable or otherwise, and with or without coupons or interest certificates thereto
-- attached, to an amount sufficient with its capital stock to provide for all the payments it will be required to make, or obligations it will
-- be required to assume, in order to effect the merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication."
-- READING F-260-1: "to an amount sufficient with its capital stock to provide for all the payments" is a limit: the bonds and obligations may be
-- issued up to the amount that, with the capital stock, covers what the corporation must pay or assume. (The other reading, that "sufficient"
-- names only the purpose and sets no ceiling, is recorded in the fork register.) The capital stock is the corporation's capital in dollars.
-- src:1236 | (a) When 2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes domesticated as, a corporation of this State, the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation or upon conversion or domestication may issue bonds or other obligations, negotiable or otherwise, and with or without coupons or interest certificates thereto attached, to an amount sufficient with its capital stock to provide for all the payments it will be required to make, or obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 260(a) (src:1236)
GIVEN `the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` IS A NUMBER
      `the capital stock of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 260(a) the most the corporation may issue in bonds or other obligations` `the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` `the capital stock of the corporation` MEANS
    max 0 (`the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` MINUS `the capital stock of the corporation`)

-- src:1236 | (a) When 2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes domesticated as, a corporation of this State, the corporation surviving or resulting from the merger or consolidation or upon conversion or domestication may issue bonds or other obligations, negotiable or otherwise, and with or without coupons or interest certificates thereto attached, to an amount sufficient with its capital stock to provide for all the payments it will be required to make, or obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the merger, consolidation, conversion or domestication …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 260(a) (src:1236)
GIVEN `2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes domesticated as, a corporation of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the bonds or other obligations to be issued` IS A NUMBER
      `the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` IS A NUMBER
      `the capital stock of the corporation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 260(a) the corporation may issue bonds or other obligations in this amount` `2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes domesticated as, a corporation of this State` `the amount of the bonds or other obligations to be issued` `the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` `the capital stock of the corporation` MEANS
        `2 or more corporations are merged or consolidated, or an other entity is converted to, or a non-United States entity becomes domesticated as, a corporation of this State`
    AND `the amount of the bonds or other obligations to be issued` AT LEAST 0
    AND `the amount of the bonds or other obligations to be issued` AT MOST `s 260(a) the most the corporation may issue in bonds or other obligations` `the payments the corporation will be required to make, and the obligations it will be required to assume, in order to effect the transaction` `the capital stock of the corporation`

-- (b) "For the purpose of securing the payment of any bonds and obligations issued under subsection (a) of this section, the surviving,
-- resulting, converted or domesticated corporation may mortgage its corporate franchise, rights, privileges and property, real, personal or mixed."
-- src:1237 | (b) For the purpose of securing the payment of any bonds and obligations issued under subsection (a) of this section, the surviving, resulting, converted or domesticated corporation may mortgage its corporate franchise, rights, privileges and property, real, personal or mixed …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 260(b) (src:1237)
GIVEN `the mortgage is for the purpose of securing the payment of bonds and obligations issued under subsection (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 260(b) the corporation may mortgage its corporate franchise, rights, privileges and property` `the mortgage is for the purpose of securing the payment of bonds and obligations issued under subsection (a)` MEANS
    `the mortgage is for the purpose of securing the payment of bonds and obligations issued under subsection (a)`

-- (c) "The surviving, resulting, converting or domesticated corporation may take any of the following actions in order to effect the merger or
-- consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement or in order to effect the conversion or domestication in the manner
-- and on the terms, pursuant to a plan of conversion or plan of domestication, approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity,
-- as applicable: (1) Issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights, or
-- securities of or interests in any constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity. (2) Cancel any
-- shares, rights, securities, or interests."
-- src:1238 | (c) The surviving, resulting, converting or domesticated corporation may take any of the following actions in order to effect the merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement or in order to effect the conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms, pursuant to a plan of conversion or plan of domestication, approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity, as applicable:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 260(c) (src:1238)
DECLARE `s 260(c) Action the corporation takes to effect the transaction` IS ONE OF
    `issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity`
    `cancel any shares, rights, securities or interests`

-- src:1238 | (c) The surviving, resulting, converting or domesticated corporation may take any of the following actions in order to effect the merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement or in order to effect the conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms, pursuant to a plan of conversion or plan of domestication, approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity, as applicable:
-- src:1239 | (1) Issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights, or securities of or interests in any constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity …
-- src:1240 | (2) Cancel any shares, rights, securities, or interests.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 260(c) (src:1238-1240)
GIVEN action IS A `s 260(c) Action the corporation takes to effect the transaction`
      `the action is taken in order to effect a merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is taken in order to effect a conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms of a plan approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares or securities are issued upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 260(c) the corporation may take the action` action `the action is taken in order to effect a merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement` `the action is taken in order to effect a conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms of a plan approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity` `the shares or securities are issued upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity` MEANS
        (   `the action is taken in order to effect a merger or consolidation in the manner and on the terms specified in the agreement`
         OR `the action is taken in order to effect a conversion or domestication in the manner and on the terms of a plan approved by the other entity or the non-United States entity`)
    AND (CONSIDER action
         WHEN `issue shares of its capital stock and other securities upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity` THEN `the shares or securities are issued upon conversion of or in exchange for the shares, rights or securities of, or interests in, a constituent corporation, converting other entity or domesticating non-United States entity`
         WHEN `cancel any shares, rights, securities or interests` THEN TRUE)

§ `s 261 Remedies; stockholder representatives; effect of a merger upon pending actions`

-- (a) "Any agreement of merger or consolidation governed by s 251 of this title, other than a merger effected pursuant to s 251(g), s 252,
-- s 254, s 255, s 256, s 257, s 258, s 263 or s 264 of this title, may provide:". Fork F-261-1 (NOTES.md): the words are read as one list of
-- the sections whose mergers proceed by an "agreement of merger or consolidation" (ss 251, 252, 254 to 258, 263, 264), with the one carve-out
-- of a merger under s 251(g); so the provisions below are open to the agreement of a merger under any of them, including the nonstock mergers of
-- ss 255 to 258 that this piece encodes, and to no merger under s 251(g), s 253, s 267 or the conversion and transfer sections (ss 266, 390).
-- The other reading, that everything after "other than" is excluded, would shut ss 252 and 254 to 258, 263, 264 out and leave s 251 alone; the
-- register records it and the reasons for not taking it.
-- src:1244 | (a) Any agreement of merger or consolidation governed by § 251 of this title, other than a merger effected pursuant to § 251(g), § 252, § 254, § 255, § 256, § 257, § 258, § 263 or § 264 of this title may provide:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a) (src:1244)
GIVEN p IS A `dg7 Provision under which a transaction is effected`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a) the agreement may contain the provisions of this subsection` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 251 other than a merger under s 251(g)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger under s 251(g)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 252` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger of a parent corporation and its subsidiary under s 253` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 254` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 255` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 256` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 257` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 258` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 263` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a merger or consolidation under s 264` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a conversion under s 266` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a merger of a parent entity and its subsidiary under s 267` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a transfer, domestication or continuance under s 390` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a transaction effected under none of the provisions that s 261 and s 262 name` THEN FALSE

-- (a)(1)(i) "a party to the agreement that fails to perform its obligations under such agreement in accordance with the terms and conditions of
-- such agreement, or that otherwise fails to comply with the terms and conditions of such agreement, in each case, required to be performed or
-- complied with prior to the time such merger or consolidation becomes effective, or that otherwise fails to consummate, or fails to cause the
-- consummation of, the merger or consolidation ... shall be subject, in addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, to such
-- penalties or consequences as are set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation".
-- src:1245 | (1) That (i) a party to the agreement that fails to perform its obligations under such agreement in accordance with the terms and conditions of such agreement, or that otherwise fails to comply with the terms and conditions of such agreement, in each case, required to be performed or complied with prior to the time such merger or consolidation becomes effective, or that otherwise fails to consummate, or fails to cause the consummation of, the merger or consolidation (whether prior to a specified date, upon satisfaction or, to the extent permitted by law, waiver of all conditions to such consummation set forth in such agreement, or otherwise) shall be subject, in addition to any other remedies available at law or in equity, to such penalties or consequences as are set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a)(1) (src:1245)
GIVEN `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement sets forth penalties or consequences for the failure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party failed to perform its obligations under the agreement in accordance with its terms, in each case required to be performed before the merger becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party otherwise failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the agreement, in each case required to be complied with before the merger becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party otherwise failed to consummate, or to cause the consummation of, the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a)(1) the party is subject to the penalties or consequences set forth in the agreement` `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` `the agreement sets forth penalties or consequences for the failure` `the party failed to perform its obligations under the agreement in accordance with its terms, in each case required to be performed before the merger becomes effective` `the party otherwise failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the agreement, in each case required to be complied with before the merger becomes effective` `the party otherwise failed to consummate, or to cause the consummation of, the merger or consolidation` MEANS
        `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)`
    AND `the agreement sets forth penalties or consequences for the failure`
    AND (   `the party failed to perform its obligations under the agreement in accordance with its terms, in each case required to be performed before the merger becomes effective`
         OR `the party otherwise failed to comply with the terms and conditions of the agreement, in each case required to be complied with before the merger becomes effective`
         OR `the party otherwise failed to consummate, or to cause the consummation of, the merger or consolidation`)

-- "(which penalties or consequences may include an obligation to pay to the other party or parties to such agreement an amount representing,
-- or based on the loss of, any premium or other economic entitlement the stockholders of such other party would be entitled to receive pursuant
-- to the terms of such agreement if the merger or consolidation were consummated in accordance with the terms of such agreement)".
-- src:1245 | (which penalties or consequences may include an obligation to pay to the other party or parties to such agreement an amount representing, or based on the loss of, any premium or other economic entitlement the stockholders of such other party would be entitled to receive pursuant to the terms of such agreement if the merger or consolidation were consummated in accordance with the terms of such agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a)(1) (src:1245)
GIVEN `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a)(1) the penalties or consequences may include an amount based on the loss of the premium or other economic entitlement of the stockholders` `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` MEANS
    `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)`

-- "(ii) if, pursuant to the terms of such agreement, a corporation is entitled to receive payment from another party to an agreement of merger or
-- consolidation of any amount representing such a penalty or consequence ..., such corporation shall be entitled to enforce the other party's
-- payment obligation and, upon receipt of any such payment, shall be entitled to retain the amount of such payment so received."
-- src:1245 | and (ii) if, pursuant to the terms of such agreement, a corporation is entitled to receive payment from another party to an agreement of merger or consolidation of any amount representing such a penalty or consequence (as specified in clause (i) of this paragraph (a)(1)), such corporation shall be entitled to enforce the other party’s payment obligation and, upon receipt of any such payment, shall be entitled to retain the amount of such payment so received …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a)(1) (src:1245)
GIVEN `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the terms of the agreement the corporation is entitled to receive payment from another party of an amount representing such a penalty or consequence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a)(1) the corporation may enforce the other party's payment obligation and retain the payment received` `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` `under the terms of the agreement the corporation is entitled to receive payment from another party of an amount representing such a penalty or consequence` MEANS
        `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)`
    AND `under the terms of the agreement the corporation is entitled to receive payment from another party of an amount representing such a penalty or consequence`

-- (a)(2) "(i) For the appointment, at or after the time at which the agreement of merger or consolidation is adopted by the stockholders of a
-- constituent corporation ..., of 1 or more persons (which may include the surviving or resulting entity or any officer, manager, representative
-- or agent thereof) as representative of the stockholders of a constituent corporation of this State, including those whose shares of capital
-- stock shall be cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger or consolidation and for the delegation to such person or persons of the sole and
-- exclusive authority to take action on behalf of such stockholders pursuant to such agreement, including taking such actions as the
-- representative determines to enforce (including by entering into settlements with respect to) the rights of such stockholders under the
-- agreement of merger or consolidation, on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the agreement, (ii) that any appointment
-- pursuant to clause (i) of this paragraph (a)(2) shall be irrevocable and binding on all such stockholders from and after the adoption of the
-- agreement of merger or consolidation by the requisite vote of such stockholders pursuant to this subchapter".
-- src:1246 | (2) (i) For the appointment, at or after the time at which the agreement of merger or consolidation is adopted by the stockholders of a constituent corporation to such merger or consolidation in accordance with the requirements of this subchapter, of 1 or more persons (which may include the surviving or resulting entity or any officer, manager, representative or agent thereof) as representative of the stockholders of a constituent corporation of this State, including those whose shares of capital stock shall be cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger or consolidation and for the delegation to such person or persons of the sole and exclusive authority to take action on behalf of such stockholders pursuant to such agreement, including taking such actions as the representative determines to enforce (including by entering into settlements with respect to) the rights of such stockholders under the agreement of merger or consolidation, on the terms and subject to the conditions set forth in the agreement, (ii) that any appointment pursuant to clause (i) of this paragraph (a)(2) shall be irrevocable and binding on all such stockholders from and after the adoption of the agreement of merger or consolidation by the requisite vote of such stockholders pursuant to this subchapter …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a)(2) (src:1246)
GIVEN `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides for the appointment of one or more persons as representative of the stockholders of a constituent corporation of this State, with the sole and exclusive authority to take action on their behalf pursuant to the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides that the appointment is irrevocable and binding on all such stockholders from and after the adoption of the agreement by the requisite vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholders have adopted the agreement by the requisite vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation of this State, including one whose shares are cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a)(2) the appointment of the stockholder representative binds the stockholder` `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)` `the agreement provides for the appointment of one or more persons as representative of the stockholders of a constituent corporation of this State, with the sole and exclusive authority to take action on their behalf pursuant to the agreement` `the agreement provides that the appointment is irrevocable and binding on all such stockholders from and after the adoption of the agreement by the requisite vote` `the stockholders have adopted the agreement by the requisite vote` `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation of this State, including one whose shares are cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger` MEANS
        `the agreement may contain the provisions of s 261(a)`
    AND `the agreement provides for the appointment of one or more persons as representative of the stockholders of a constituent corporation of this State, with the sole and exclusive authority to take action on their behalf pursuant to the agreement`
    AND `the agreement provides that the appointment is irrevocable and binding on all such stockholders from and after the adoption of the agreement by the requisite vote`
    AND `the stockholders have adopted the agreement by the requisite vote`
    AND `the person is a stockholder of a constituent corporation of this State, including one whose shares are cancelled, converted or exchanged in the merger`

-- "(iii) that any provision adopted pursuant to this paragraph (a)(2) may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective
-- or may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons specified in the agreement of merger or consolidation."
-- Before the transaction is effective the paragraph says nothing about amendment (s 251(d) governs, piece dg6): NOTHING (not covered).
-- src:1246 | and (iii) that any provision adopted pursuant to this paragraph (a)(2) may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective or may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons specified in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a)(2) (src:1246)
GIVEN `the merger or consolidation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides that the provision may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement provides that the provision may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons it specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the persons specified have consented to or approved the amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 261(a)(2) the provision may be amended` `the merger or consolidation has become effective` `the agreement provides that the provision may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective` `the agreement provides that the provision may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons it specifies` `the persons specified have consented to or approved the amendment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the merger or consolidation has become effective`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the agreement provides that the provision may not be amended after the merger or consolidation has become effective`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST (       `the agreement provides that the provision may be amended only with the consent or approval of persons it specifies`
                     AND `the persons specified have consented to or approved the amendment`)

-- "Any provision of the agreement of merger or consolidation adopted pursuant to this subsection may be made dependent upon facts (including,
-- but not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation)
-- ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly
-- and expressly set forth in the agreement". (The parenthesis defining "facts" is inert, KEEL instruction 15.)
-- src:1247 | Any provision of the agreement of merger or consolidation adopted pursuant to this subsection may be made dependent upon facts (including, but not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation) ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(a) (src:1247)
GIVEN `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(a) a provision may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement` MEANS
    `the manner in which the facts operate upon the terms is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement`

-- (b) "Any action or proceeding, whether civil, criminal or administrative, pending by or against any corporation which is a party to a merger or
-- consolidation shall be prosecuted as if such merger or consolidation had not taken place, or the corporation surviving or resulting from such
-- merger or consolidation may be substituted in such action or proceeding."
-- src:1248 | (b) Any action or proceeding, whether civil, criminal or administrative, pending by or against any corporation which is a party to a merger or consolidation shall be prosecuted as if such merger or consolidation had not taken place, or the corporation surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation may be substituted in such action or proceeding …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 261(b) (src:1248)
GIVEN `the action or proceeding, civil, criminal or administrative, is pending by or against a corporation that is a party to the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merger or consolidation has taken place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 261(b) the pending action or proceeding is prosecuted as if the merger or consolidation had not taken place` `the action or proceeding, civil, criminal or administrative, is pending by or against a corporation that is a party to the merger or consolidation` `the merger or consolidation has taken place` MEANS
        `the action or proceeding, civil, criminal or administrative, is pending by or against a corporation that is a party to the merger or consolidation`
    AND `the merger or consolidation has taken place`

